 "posts": [
  "NEGROS POWER ADVISORY\nMANUAL LOAD DROPPING (MLD) SCHEDULE \nOctober 21, 2026 (Wednesday)\nDue to the alert levels declared by the National Grid Corporation of the Philippines (NGCP) today, Distribution Utilities (DUs) in the Visayas, including Negros Power, have been directed to implement possible power interruptions through Manual Load Dropping (MLD). \nAs per NGCP, in their advisory today via https:https://www.facebook.com/share/p/193FckwQj3/, Due to limited generation supply from Mindanao.\nFactor/s that contributed to the RED and YELLOW Alert declarations:\n1. Unavailability of Visayas' large coal plants TVI 1, TVI 2, and PEDC 3\n2. Limited power import from the Mindanao Grid\nAt present, the following feeders are being considered for possible MLD implementation (refer to the photo provided). \nPlease be advised that the schedule, duration, and affected feeders may change at any time, depending on the actual condition of the power system and/or further directives from NGCP.\nNegros Power continues to closely coordinate with NGCP and will provide updates as necessary.\nTo know which feeder you are connected, please refer to the link: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/18oNLoVaqA/\nFor the latest information and updates, please refer to the official posts of Negros Power on our Facebook page. We encourage the public to regularly check our official posts for any changes to the MLD schedule, affected feeders, and other related advisories.\nWe sincerely ask for your understanding, patience, and cooperation as these measures are being implemented to help maintain the stability of the power grid.\n#NegrosPower #VisayasGrid #NGCP #AlertLevels #ManualLoadDrop"
 ],
